guage and a lot  of the [ __ ] that hannibal is saying  are words that i have to look up to go  like is that right like is that a word  and so i it was it was really difficult  for him  um but we kind of like the first season  was really was  was insane and it was very depressing  and  it felt very much like uh i was in will  graham's head a little too far  uh and i remember there like there was  one time when um  hugh and claire and i were walking  around a park  and it was just like it was just nice to  be  with people who weren't  expecting something from me that i knew  i couldn't give them  and to just have general support and go  like oh like these like i said like  when when you and i had our first dinner  i was like oh  this this is going to be my friend like  this isn't just a working relationship  this is somebody that who's company that  i adore  so like those moments kind of got me  through  the complexities and the real  hardships of season one and then after  surviving something you'll go like oh i  can survive  but season two we got a late pickup  and so our first day in the writers room  without  anything being sort of written or  anything  we were in production six weeks later  and  so they're like there was no catching up  and season two i don't know  hugh if you think season two was worse  than season one in terms of script  delivery  it's hard to say they're so  i mean yeah it's it's it's kind of  really  skinning something but it was it was it  was tough  all along and and yeah that's that's all  i know i mean  in that respect but you know i did i i  worked after hannibal i worked on a show  and  in the first ep season we had all six  six episodes they'd written of 10 i  think we did up front they just had you  know that much time and they had they'd  scripted those six episodes and it was  great i mean it was completely  wild it was almost like a hallucination  for me  um and you know it meant it afforded me  the opportunity to  i guess you kno